# Binary assets are committed directly. They were Git LFS for a while, when
# the dummy avatar pack alone was ~19MB of PNG; the pack is generated art now
# and the whole of it is about 3MB, which is a size git holds without help.
#
# Dropping LFS also dropped what came with it: a pre-push hook that refused to
# push without git-lfs installed, a checkout that handed actool pointer text
# and took the build down with it, and a second place where old asset versions
# lived on after the history had been rewritten.
*.png binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.m4a binary
